{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>This is the instruction of the zav.</b> This is what is proper to examine in all these: first, that the zav requiring a sin-offering indicates that he has committed a sin in deed and in thought." "<b>And if a flow of seed issues from him, it defiles thereby.</b> For indeed the reason for the impurity of a discharge is that the intention of the one emitting it is for defilement therein, in the serpent's craving — not for the perpetuation of the species. Were it not for this, there would be no impurity in the seed whatsoever, just as there is no impurity in excrement and urine."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:38.066485235Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}